CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "17f884f4-9cd3-424e-ab5c-cc1157efaa48",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T16:09:24Z",
  "ticket_id": "4ba1-759f",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "Brainstorm Phase 1 context loading includes a structured scale-evidence lookup \u2014 check design-notes.md and project configs/constants first, then perform a domain web search for volume estimates, then ask the user only if neither yields a usable estimate (defined as: a numeric order-of-magnitude value, or an explicit statement that volume is negligible or unbounded) \u2014 this lookup runs whenever the feature description implies a volume-sensitive decision (e.g., processing records, serving traffic, querying a data store)",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior for how the brainstorm phase handles context loading, phrased as ongoing operational procedure"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Brainstorm Phase 2 approach proposals always include at least one simple baseline option; any approach that adds a library dependency, performance optimization, or abstraction referenced by fewer than three existing call sites (Rule of Three) or that introduces a new interface, base class, or protocol type must cite the evidence that warrants it (scale evidence from the lookup, a confirmed user requirement, a correctness/security rationale, or an explicit user statement)",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable policy for how the system evaluates and documents design proposals going forward, phrased as an ongoing requirement"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "scale-inference.md exists in plugins/dso/skills/shared/prompts/, defines the artifacts to domain web search to ask protocol, and is read by brainstorm Phase 1; if the file cannot be read at runtime, brainstorm emits an explicit error naming the missing file rather than silently proceeding",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior (file existence, error handling) that persists after completion rather than a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "complexity-gate.md exists in plugins/dso/skills/shared/prompts/, defines the six complexity gates (YAGNI, profiling-first, Rule of Three, dependency cost/benefit, scale threshold, LLM self-audit), and is read by both brainstorm Phase 2 and implementation-plan task proposal phase; if the file cannot be read, the calling skill emits an explicit error naming the missing file",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property (file existence and accessibility) that enables ongoing behavior in multiple phases, phrased as a state condition rather than a completed task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The approach-decision-maker agent Dimension 4 (Simplicity) rationale explicitly names which complexity-gate rule applied to each flagged proposal \u2014 when a proposal is flagged as over-engineered, the rationale includes the specific gate violated; when no gate fires, the rationale notes that the proposal satisfies all complexity gates",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where the agent produces rationales that explicitly name complexity-gate rules, an ongoing property that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A dogfooding validation confirms behavioral change: running brainstorm on a volume-sensitive feature description confirms (a) Phase 1 performs the scale-evidence lookup step, (b) Phase 2 includes a simple baseline option, and (c) any approach proposing a library dependency or performance optimization includes an evidence citation \u2014 verified against a checklist before epic closure",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time validation task completed before epic closure, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
